From: ENIAC Touch Kiosk <kiosk@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] mult: print the multiplier stage without padding

multstat() formats the stage as "%2d ", so a stage below 10 gets a
leading space ("m  0 ..."). Consumers that split on single spaces
(vis/eniactk.go) index an empty field and panic the first time the
multiplier runs. Print "%d " instead. Reported upstream (see #34).

---
diff --git a/src/mult.go b/src/mult.go
--- a/src/mult.go
+++ b/src/mult.go
@@ -63,7 +63,7 @@
 }
 
 func multstat() string {
-	s := fmt.Sprintf("%2d ", stage)
+	s := fmt.Sprintf("%d ", stage)
 	for i, _ := range multff {
 		if multff[i] {
 			s += "1"
